WEBVTT

00:00:00.382 --> 00:00:09.662
In this video, we'll change the practice FAQ from the last video, make a copy of it, take it down for a while, and then delete it.

00:00:10.229 --> 00:00:17.919
To edit an entry, find it in its collection, or type a few words into Search all and press Enter.

00:00:17.919 --> 00:00:19.029
Then click it.

00:00:19.587 --> 00:00:20.858
Change any field.

00:00:20.858 --> 00:00:23.250
Here, we'll reword the question.

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:28.707
The status turns to Unsaved changes, and the button goes back to Publish.

00:00:29.261 --> 00:00:30.610
Publish now saves it.

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:34.851
Note that changing the question doesn't change the page's address.

00:00:34.851 --> 00:00:41.341
It keeps the one it was given when first published, so links people have already shared keep working.

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:44.762
Changing an FAQ's topic is different.

00:00:44.762 --> 00:00:49.529
It moves the FAQ to the new topic's list, and changes its address.

00:00:49.529 --> 00:00:55.090
If an address really must change, ask Thothica, who can redirect the old one.

00:00:55.651 --> 00:01:03.651
To start a new FAQ that's close to an existing one, open the Published menu, and choose Duplicate.

00:01:04.203 --> 00:01:08.337
You get a new, unsaved copy, with every field filled in.

00:01:08.337 --> 00:01:11.363
Change the question before publishing it.

00:01:11.932 --> 00:01:15.406
If a required field is empty, nothing is saved.

00:01:15.406 --> 00:01:18.732
Let's clear the question, and try to publish.

00:01:19.283 --> 00:01:22.578
A red notice says you've missed a required field.

00:01:22.578 --> 00:01:27.486
Scroll up to find the field marked in red, fill it in, and publish again.

00:01:27.486 --> 00:01:34.883
A field with a value in the wrong format is refused the same way, and the message under it says what it wants.

00:01:35.443 --> 00:01:38.384
We don't want this copy, so we'll leave it.

00:01:38.384 --> 00:01:43.444
Because it isn't saved, the browser asks if you're sure you want to leave.

00:01:43.444 --> 00:01:46.043
Click OK, and the copy is thrown away.

00:01:46.751 --> 00:01:52.007
To take a page down for now, open it, switch Draft on, and publish.

00:01:52.007 --> 00:01:54.674
The page disappears from the site.

00:01:54.674 --> 00:01:58.831
To bring it back, switch Draft off and publish again.

00:01:59.543 --> 00:02:05.943
With Draft on, the page shows Page not found, and nothing else about it has changed.

00:02:06.822 --> 00:02:08.613
Deleting is a last resort.

00:02:08.613 --> 00:02:15.778
Every link to the deleted page, from other sites and from shared messages, then lands on Page not found.

00:02:15.778 --> 00:02:18.533
And images uploaded into it stay behind.

00:02:18.533 --> 00:02:24.182
If you delete something by mistake, Thothica can restore it from GitHub's history.

00:02:24.736 --> 00:02:27.039
To delete, click Delete entry.

00:02:27.039 --> 00:02:32.565
The browser asks if you're sure you want to delete this published entry.

00:02:32.565 --> 00:02:33.256
Click OK.

00:02:33.809 --> 00:02:37.198
You're back in the list, and the FAQ is gone.

00:02:37.198 --> 00:02:43.449
On the live site, its page disappears at the next rebuild, about two minutes later.

00:02:44.166 --> 00:02:46.606
Next: adding a video.
